 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Norwegian letters",
     "texto": [
      "The Norwegian alphabet uses Latin letters and ends with three extra letters: æ, ø and å, in that order. **Æ** sounds like the «a» in «cat»; **ø** is pronounced with rounded lips and has no exact equivalent in English; **å** sounds roughly like the vowel in «go», without the «w».",
      "In Norwegian, names are usually spelled the same way, even though their pronunciation cannot always be worked out letter by letter. To ask someone to spell a name: Kan du stave navnet ditt? («Can you spell your name?»).",
      "Kan is followed by the infinitive without å: kan stave, not kan å stave. Navn is neuter; its definite form is navnet («the name»), with the article added at the end of the noun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
